# Text files are LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This project is checked out on Windows, built there, and run on macOS and Linux.
# The Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) writes CRLF into a fresh checkout, and a
# CRLF checkout breaks this repository in ways that never show up in the diff:
#
#   scripts/*.sh, scripts/release/*.sh   run under bash on CI and on macOS releases
#   apps/desktop/src-tauri/shell-integration/{bash-rcfile,zsh/*}
#                                        sourced verbatim by the user's shells
#
# A CRLF shell script works on the machine it was cloned on and fails on the one
# that actually runs it. Pin every text file to LF instead of relying on each
# contributor's autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets, explicit so a later attribute change cannot rewrite their bytes.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.webp binary